our operations, including an unprecedented decline in demand, as well as its current, and uncertain future impact, including but not
limited to, its effect on the ability or desire of people to travel due to travel restrictions, and other restrictions and orders, which is
expected to continue to impact our results, operations, outlooks, plans, goals, growth, cash flows, liquidity, and stock price;
• the high level of competition in the mobility industry, including from new companies or technology, and the impact such competition
may have on pricing and rental volume;
• a change in our fleet costs, including as a result of a change in the cost of new vehicles, manufacturer recalls, disruption in the
supply of new vehicles, and/or a change in the price at which we dispose of used vehicles either in the used vehicle market or under
repurchase or guaranteed depreciation programs;
• our ability to realize our estimated cost savings on a timely basis, or at all, and the amount of cash expenditures made in connection
with such cost saving efforts;
• the results of operations or financial condition of the manufacturers of our vehicles, which could impact their ability to perform their
